    {
      "id": "t011104",
      "source": "Problem 636. Earth, sunlight, and local time: case 1",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011105",
      "source": "Knowledge context.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011106",
      "source": "Earth–Sun relationships explain broad patterns such as day length and local time, but a problem should state the simplified model it expects children to use.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011107",
      "source": "Given facts.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011108",
      "source": "For this classroom model, Eastport is 1 time zone(s) east of Westport. Each zone east is one hour later. At Westport it is 11:00.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011109",
      "source": "Rules.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011110",
      "source": "Moving east adds one hour per stated time zone; moving west subtracts. Use the given model only.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011111",
      "source": "Task.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011112",
      "source": "What local time is it in Eastport?",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011113",
      "source": "Step-by-step solution.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011114",
      "source": "1. Time difference is +1 hour(s) because Eastport is east. 2. 11+1=12 (mod 24).",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "t011115",
      "source": "Answer.",
      "translation": ""
    },
    {
